"Physical input mix → input trim → effects in listed order → drift → output gain → physical outputs. Add installed stereo Audio Units, reorder them, or open Edit to adjust their parameters.\n\nTurning Enable effect processing off fades to dry audio over 20 ms, then stops plugin render calls. Loaded effects remain editable; their signal meters and DSP state pause once the fade finishes. The helper and queues stay active in both modes. Starting with processing off loads no plugins; enabling prepares the saved chain while dry audio continues, then fades it in without restarting either device. The switch is saved; changes during preparation are reconciled when startup finishes. Manual Stop still stops the bridge. Queued audio finishes normally. A fade reduces abrupt level changes but does not align the dry signal with plugin latency, erase plugin tails or guarantee inaudible transitions for every effect.\n\nBypass fades to dry audio while effects remain processing, retaining live signal feedback in editors. The bypass preference is preserved while processing is off. Live inserts switch at a processing boundary; audible transitions are possible. A live editor controls the rendering instance; close it to save its settings. Stopped editors save settings for the next Start.\n\n" = "Physical input mix → input trim → effects in listed order → drift → output gain → physical outputs. Add installed stereo Audio Units, reorder them, or open Edit to adjust their parameters.\n\nTurning Enable effect processing off fades to dry audio over 20 ms, then stops plugin render calls. Loaded effects remain editable; their signal meters and DSP state pause once the fade finishes. The helper and queues stay active in both modes. Starting with processing off loads no plugins; enabling prepares the saved chain while dry audio continues, then fades it in without restarting either device. The switch is saved; changes during preparation are reconciled when startup finishes. Manual Stop still stops the bridge. Queued audio finishes normally. A fade reduces abrupt level changes but does not align the dry signal with plugin latency, erase plugin tails or guarantee inaudible transitions for every effect.\n\nBypass fades to dry audio while effects remain processing, retaining live signal feedback in editors. The bypass preference is preserved while processing is off. Live inserts switch at a processing boundary; audible transitions are possible. A live editor controls the rendering instance; close it to save its settings. Stopped editors save settings for the next Start.\n\n";
