"Reserve is your FIFO setting. Allocated capacity (minimum 1024 frames) is storage headroom, not another latency setting or a queue filled to that size. The bridge uses separate capture and ready queues, each with this capacity, including when DSP is off. Pending source counts accepted audio across those queues and the in-flight block without adding the reserve again. Unused capacity adds no audio delay.\n\nThe timestamp-derived clock difference is separate from the occupancy controller's correction command. FIFO occupancy naturally changes between callbacks. A correction value alone is not evidence of lost audio or a physical clock fault. Individual queue snapshots are approximate. A backlog can remain after DSP is switched off; dry forwarding keeps the queued audio rather than silently dropping it to lower the delay." = "Reserve is your FIFO setting. Allocated capacity (minimum 1024 frames) is storage headroom, not another latency setting or a queue filled to that size. The bridge uses separate capture and ready queues, each with this capacity, including when DSP is off. Pending source counts accepted audio across those queues and the in-flight block without adding the reserve again. Unused capacity adds no audio delay.\n\nThe timestamp-derived clock difference is separate from the occupancy controller's correction command. FIFO occupancy naturally changes between callbacks. A correction value alone is not evidence of lost audio or a physical clock fault. Individual queue snapshots are approximate. A backlog can remain after DSP is switched off; dry forwarding keeps the queued audio rather than silently dropping it to lower the delay.";
