"The switch starts/stops only HTTP. Settings save automatically. Cycle this switch after changing its port; regenerated tokens take effect immediately.\n\nStatus: GET http://<Mac-IP>:%lld/api/v1/status\nControl: POST http://<Mac-IP>:%lld/api/v1/control\nHeader: Authorization: Bearer <token>\n\nStatus includes endpoint names, routing state, linear meter peaks, gains in dB and chain bypass. OutputGain controls digital fallback only; it is rejected when writable device volume is available or its capability check is pending. Status includes outputLevelControl, applied outputGainDB and saved outputFallbackGainDB. Control JSON: {\"command\":\"start\"}, {\"command\":\"stop\"}, {\"command\":\"inputGain\",\"decibels\":-6}, {\"command\":\"outputGain\",\"decibels\":0}, {\"command\":\"chainBypass\",\"bypassed\":true}.\n\nHTTP has no encryption. Use a trusted LAN; macOS firewall/privacy may affect reachability. Tokens are stored in Keychain. No audio is sent.\n\nService report: %@" = "The switch starts/stops only HTTP. Settings save automatically. Cycle this switch after changing its port; regenerated tokens take effect immediately.\n\nStatus: GET http://<Mac-IP>:%lld/api/v1/status\nControl: POST http://<Mac-IP>:%lld/api/v1/control\nHeader: Authorization: Bearer <token>\n\nStatus includes endpoint names, routing state, linear meter peaks, gains in dB and chain bypass. OutputGain controls digital fallback only; it is rejected when writable device volume is available or its capability check is pending. Status includes outputLevelControl, applied outputGainDB and saved outputFallbackGainDB. Control JSON: {\"command\":\"start\"}, {\"command\":\"stop\"}, {\"command\":\"inputGain\",\"decibels\":-6}, {\"command\":\"outputGain\",\"decibels\":0}, {\"command\":\"chainBypass\",\"bypassed\":true}.\n\nHTTP has no encryption. Use a trusted LAN; macOS firewall/privacy may affect reachability. Tokens are stored in Keychain. No audio is sent.\n\nService report: %@";
"The switch starts/stops only OSC. Settings save automatically. Cycle this switch after changing its port or Companion destination; allowlist edits take effect immediately. Commands are accepted only from exact allowlisted source IPs.\n\nCommands: /audiobridge/start, /audiobridge/stop (no arguments); /audiobridge/input/gain, /audiobridge/output/gain (float dB); /audiobridge/effects/bypass (integer 0 or 1).\n\nFeedback is sent every second to Companion: /audiobridge/status (string), /audiobridge/running (integer), /audiobridge/input/left, /audiobridge/input/right, /audiobridge/output/left, /audiobridge/output/right (float linear peaks).\n\nOSC has no cryptographic authentication. Use a trusted LAN. macOS firewall and Local Network privacy can affect delivery. No audio is sent.\n\nService report: %@" = "The switch starts/stops only OSC. Settings save automatically. Cycle this switch after changing its port or Companion destination; allowlist edits take effect immediately. Commands are accepted only from exact allowlisted source IPs.\n\nCommands: /audiobridge/start, /audiobridge/stop (no arguments); /audiobridge/input/gain, /audiobridge/output/gain (float dB); /audiobridge/effects/bypass (integer 0 or 1).\n\nFeedback is sent every second to Companion: /audiobridge/status (string), /audiobridge/running (integer), /audiobridge/input/left, /audiobridge/input/right, /audiobridge/output/left, /audiobridge/output/right (float linear peaks).\n\nOSC has no cryptographic authentication. Use a trusted LAN. macOS firewall and Local Network privacy can affect delivery. No audio is sent.\n\nService report: %@";
"These are driver-reported capabilities and stream formats. Device UID is the saved selection identity; runtime stream identifiers may change. This read-only report does not open or test audio delivery. Expand stream rows to inspect their virtual and physical formats." = "These are driver-reported capabilities and stream formats. Device UID is the saved selection identity; runtime stream identifiers may change. This read-only report does not open or test audio delivery. Expand stream rows to inspect their virtual and physical formats.";
