"These are the same Mix L and Mix R buses after effects, drift compensation and output gain. Patch either bus to as many physical outputs on the selected device as needed. Each output takes one side; right-click a row for an explicit mono L+R sum or disconnect. Summing can clip. No physical output is silently selected." = "These are the same Mix L and Mix R buses after effects, drift compensation and output gain. Patch either bus to as many physical outputs on the selected device as needed. Each output takes one side; right-click a row for an explicit mono L+R sum or disconnect. Summing can clip. No physical output is silently selected.";
"This bundle is eligible for login registration." = "This bundle is eligible for login registration.";
"This is Audio Bridge's software queue, separate from each device's hardware buffer. The default target is twice the larger selected device buffer, with a 64-frame minimum (64-frame devices target 128 frames). It is saved immediately and takes effect on the next Start.\n\nRefill waits for this reserve plus one output callback and FIR lookahead. Smaller reserves reduce queue delay but leave less time for Audio Units and scheduler delays. If delivery losses increase, stop and raise the reserve. The driver buffers remain separate. Expert presets and exact values are available below; the valid minimum follows the larger device buffer, at least 16 frames. Actual delay is shown in Bridge." = "This is Audio Bridge's software queue, separate from each device's hardware buffer. The default target is twice the larger selected device buffer, with a 64-frame minimum (64-frame devices target 128 frames). It is saved immediately and takes effect on the next Start.\n\nRefill waits for this reserve plus one output callback and FIR lookahead. Smaller reserves reduce queue delay but leave less time for Audio Units and scheduler delays. If delivery losses increase, stop and raise the reserve. The driver buffers remain separate. Expert presets and exact values are available below; the valid minimum follows the larger device buffer, at least 16 frames. Actual delay is shown in Bridge.";
