"Microphone authorization covers capture from the selected audio input, including external audio interfaces. Audio Bridge does not create a system-audio tap or capture other apps or the screen, so it does not request system-audio recording permission. No authorization is inferred for features the app does not use.\n\nUse Request for the first microphone prompt; use Privacy Settings after a denial. Capture begins only when you start the configured bridge. After rebuilding an ad-hoc signed app, macOS may retain a stale entry; quit it, toggle its Microphone entry and reopen the same bundle.\n\nThe notification switch controls device-error alerts inside Audio Bridge. macOS permission is shown separately and is not revoked by turning that switch off. A device failure still stops routing and remains visible in Bridge even when notifications are denied. macOS Focus and notification presentation settings can suppress alerts despite authorization." = "Microphone authorization covers capture from the selected audio input, including external audio interfaces. Audio Bridge does not create a system-audio tap or capture other apps or the screen, so it does not request system-audio recording permission. No authorization is inferred for features the app does not use.\n\nUse Request for the first microphone prompt; use Privacy Settings after a denial. Capture begins only when you start the configured bridge. After rebuilding an ad-hoc signed app, macOS may retain a stale entry; quit it, toggle its Microphone entry and reopen the same bundle.\n\nThe notification switch controls device-error alerts inside Audio Bridge. macOS permission is shown separately and is not revoked by turning that switch off. A device failure still stops routing and remains visible in Bridge even when notifications are denied. macOS Focus and notification presentation settings can suppress alerts despite authorization.";
